From 4e18a649b70117dd8ee35fc452828ad549347a51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kaaz <nk6352@princeton.edu>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:19:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Raise two sirocco.h limits: NBINS_IN_CELL_SPEC 1000 ->
 3000, MAXSCAT 2000 -> 200000

Two independent one-line constant changes in source/sirocco.h, bundled because
each is a bare header edit with no code dependency on the other.

NBINS_IN_CELL_SPEC 1000 -> 3000: finer cell_spec_flux grid for the per-cell
mean-intensity J_nu diagnostics written by `windsave2table -xall`
(outflow.xspec.all.txt has 3001 rows). With the custom-band photon sampling
the fixed bin count spans ~3.3 decades ([0.05,100] eV) instead of ~10, so 3000
bins gives ~900 bins/decade at the Balmer/Lyman edges.

MAXSCAT 2000 -> 200000: trans_phot.c terminates any photon reaching MAXSCAT
scatters with P_TOO_MANY_SCATTERS and discards its energy. The tau_es~100
photon-tired winds need ~50k scatters per photon to escape, so the upstream
default of 2000 destroyed ~94% of the luminosity: photon fates for pt_m5 were
escape=332 / too_many_scatters=1650 (vs escape=6730 / too_many=0 with the cap
raised), giving a 20x too-faint spectrum and starving the radiation field
enough to drive spurious recombination. The marginally-unbound winds peak at
~1200 scatters and are unaffected. Check that the diagnostic "luminosity lost
by too many scatters" is 0 on thick winds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/sirocco.h | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/sirocco.h b/source/sirocco.h
index e5220fbf..4a8efd24 100644
--- a/source/sirocco.h
+++ b/source/sirocco.h
@@ -141,7 +141,13 @@ extern int NWAVE_NOW;         /**< Either NWAVE_IONIZ or NWAVE_EXTRACT depending
                                 */
 #define NWAVE_MIN   100       /**< The minimum number of wavelength bins in during spectral cycles
                                */
-#define MAXSCAT    2000
+#define MAXSCAT    200000     /**< Photons reaching this many scatters are destroyed by
+                                 trans_phot.c (P_TOO_MANY_SCATTERS), discarding their energy.
+                                 The tau_es~100 photon-tired winds need ~50k scatters per
+                                 photon to escape, so the upstream default of 2000 silently
+                                 destroys ~94% of the luminosity. Check the diagnostic
+                                 "luminosity lost by too many scatters" is 0 on thick winds.
+                                 */
 
 /* Define the structures */
 #include "math_struc.h"
@@ -567,7 +573,7 @@ struct geometry
   int nxfreq;                   /**<  the number of frequency intervals actually used */
   double xfreq[NXBANDS + 1];    /**<  the frequency boundaries for the coarse spectra  */
 
-#define NBINS_IN_CELL_SPEC   1000       /**< The number of bins in the cell spectra  */
+#define NBINS_IN_CELL_SPEC   3000       /**< The number of bins in the cell spectra  */
 
   double cell_log_freq_min, cell_log_freq_max, cell_delta_lfreq;        /**< Parameters defining freqency intervals for cell spectra.
                                                                            These are defined as logarithmic frequency intervals */
